# Design System Preview Screen

## Purpose
The Design System screen is the main app entry during development.
It shows all components with all states, organized by atomic category and Figma page.

## Structure

```
src/screens/DesignSystem/
├── index.tsx              # Main DS screen: search + tabs + list
├── registry.ts            # Component registry (auto-maintained)
├── components/
│   ├── DSComponentCard.tsx    # List item: component name + preview
│   ├── DSComponentPage.tsx    # Full page: all states of one component
│   ├── DSSearchBar.tsx        # Search input
│   ├── DSTabBar.tsx           # Category tabs (Atoms / Molecules / Organisms / by Figma page)
│   └── DSTextStressTest.tsx   # Multi-language text length tester
└── screens/
    └── DSTokensScreen.tsx     # Color tokens viewer (primitives + semantic)
```

## registry.ts Rules

This file is the source of truth for what's in the design system.

```ts
// src/screens/DesignSystem/registry.ts

import type { ComponentType } from 'react';

export type DSCategory = 'atoms' | 'molecules' | 'organisms';

export interface DSComponentEntry {
  id: string;              // kebab-case unique ID
  name: string;            // Display name — same as component name
  category: DSCategory;
  figmaPage?: string;      // Figma page this belongs to (e.g. 'Controls', 'Booking')
  description?: string;    // 1-line description
  states: DSStateEntry[];  // All states/variants to preview
  component: ComponentType<any>;
}

export interface DSStateEntry {
  label: string;           // Human-readable state label
  props: Record<string, any>; // Props to apply for this state
}

export const componentRegistry: DSComponentEntry[] = [];
```

**Cursor must update this file automatically** when:
- A new component is created → append entry
- A new state/variant is added → update `states` array for that entry
- A component is renamed → update `id` and `name`
- A component is deleted → remove entry

Example entry for `AppButton`:
```ts
{
  id: 'app-button',
  name: 'AppButton',
  category: 'atoms',
  figmaPage: 'Controls',
  description: 'Primary action button. Supports primary, secondary, ghost variants.',
  states: [
    { label: 'Primary Default', props: { variant: 'primary', size: 'large', children: 'Забронювати' } },
    { label: 'Primary Disabled', props: { variant: 'primary', size: 'large', isDisabled: true, children: 'Забронювати' } },
    { label: 'Primary Loading', props: { variant: 'primary', size: 'large', isLoading: true, children: 'Забронювати' } },
    { label: 'Secondary Default', props: { variant: 'secondary', size: 'large', children: 'Детальніше' } },
    { label: 'Ghost Default', props: { variant: 'ghost', size: 'large', children: 'Скасувати' } },
    { label: 'Small', props: { variant: 'primary', size: 'small', children: 'Фільтр' } },
    // Multi-language stress test states:
    { label: 'Long text (DE)', props: { variant: 'primary', size: 'large', children: 'Jetzt Skipass kaufen' } },
    { label: 'Long text (2 lines)', props: { variant: 'primary', size: 'large', children: 'Забронювати лижний підйомник на завтра' } },
  ],
  component: AppButton,
},
```

## Text Stress Testing

Every component entry with text content must include at minimum:
1. Default (Ukrainian, normal length)
2. Long variant (German-equivalent length — 1.5x–2x)
3. Very long variant (forces 2+ lines)

This catches layout breaks before they hit production.

## DSComponentPage Layout

When a user taps a component card in the list:
```tsx
// Shows component name, description, Figma link if available
// Then renders each state in a card with:
// - State label
// - Rendered component preview (on appropriate background)
// - Props display (collapsible JSON)
```

Background for previews:
- Use `tokens.bgOnSurface` as card background
- Render component on appropriate background per its usage context
  (e.g. a card component renders on `tokens.bgSurface`)

## Tabs in Design System Screen

Tabs let user filter by:
1. Category: `Atoms` | `Molecules` | `Organisms`
2. Figma page: populated dynamically from `figmaPage` in registry entries

Default tab: `Atoms`

## Search

Search filters by:
- Component name
- `figmaPage`
- `description`

Case-insensitive, instant filter on keystroke.

## Tokens Screen

Separate screen in DS showing:
1. Color primitives grid (all swatches from `primitives.ts`)
2. Semantic tokens table: token name | current value | swatch
3. Typography specimen: each variant with sample text
4. Spacing ruler: visual spacing scale

Accessible from DS main screen via a "Tokens" button.
